<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Synthetic Document</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  td {
    padding: 5px;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .header-section {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .title-block {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }
  .section-title {
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .instruction-list {
    list-style-type: disc;
    margin-left: 20px;
    padding-left: 0;
  }
  .instruction-list li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    font-size: 12px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <div class="header-section">
    <div>
      <strong>IRS SPECIFICATIONS</strong>
      <br>
      <strong>INSTRUCTIONS TO PRINTERS</strong>
      <br>
      FORM 4852, PAGE 1 OF 2
      <br>
      MARGINS: TOP 10 mm (0.4"), CENTER SIDES.
      <br>
      PAPER: WHITE WRITING, SUB. 20.
      <br>
      PRINT: HEAD TO HEAD
      <br>
      PERFORATE: (NONE)
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>TO BE REMOVED BEFORE PRINTING</strong>
      <br>
      PRINTS: HEAD TO HEAD
      <br>
      INK: BLACK
    </div>
  </div>
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p><strong>DO NOT PRINT — DO NOT PRINT — DO NOT PRINT — DO NOT PRINT</strong></p>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div>
      <p>Date: <span data-field="date_filed">{{ date_filed }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Action: <span data-field="action_taken">{{ action_taken }}</span></p>
      <p>Date: <span data-field="action_date">{{ action_date }}</span></p>
      <p>Signature: <span data-field="signature_name">{{ signature_name }}</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <p>Form <span data-field="form_number">{{ form_number }}</span></p>
    <p>Substitute for Form W-2, Wage and Tax Statement, or Form 1099-R, Distributions From Pensions, Annuities, Retirement or Profit-Sharing Plans, IRAs, Insurance Contracts, etc.</p>
    <p>Attach to Form 1040A, 1040E, or 1040EZ or 1040X.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>1. <span data-field="instruction_1">{{ instruction_1 }}</span></p>
    <p>2. <span data-field="instruction_2">{{ instruction_2 }}</span></p>
    <p>3. <span data-field="instruction_3">{{ instruction_3 }}</span></p>
    <p>4. <span data-field="instruction_4">{{ instruction_4 }}</span></p>
    <p>5. <span data-field="instruction_5">{{ instruction_5 }}</span></p>
    <p>6. <span data-field="instruction_6">{{ instruction_6 }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <p>7(A) Form W-2. Enter wages, tips, other compensation, and taxes withheld.</p>
    <table style="margin-top: 10px;">
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 50%;">
          <p>a. Wages, tips, and other compensation</p>
          <p>b. Social security wages</p>
          <p>c. Medicare wages and tips</p>
          <p>d. Advance EIC payment</p>
          <p>e. Social security tips</p>
          <p>f. Federal income tax withheld</p>
        </td>
        <td style="width: 50%;">
          <p>g. State income tax withheld</p>
          <p>h. Local income tax withheld</p>
          <p>i. Name of locality</p>
          <p>j. Social security tax withheld</p>
          <p>k. Medicare tax withheld</p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>7(B) Form 1099-R. Enter distributions from pensions, annuities, retirement/profit-sharing plans, IRAs, insurance contracts, etc.</p>
    <table style="margin-top: 10px;">
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 50%;">
          <p>1. Gross distribution</p>
          <p>2a. Taxable amount</p>
          <p>2b. Taxable amount not determined</p>
          <p>Total distribution</p>
          <p>3. Capital gain (included in 2a)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="width: 50%;">
          <p>4. Federal income tax withheld</p>
          <p>5. State income tax withheld</p>
          <p>6. Local income tax withheld</p>
          <p>7. Employee contributions</p>
          <p>8. Distribution codes</p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <p>8. How did you determine the amounts in lines 7(A) and 7(B) above?</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <p>9. Explain your efforts to obtain Form W-2, Form 1099-R, or Form W-2C, Corrected Wage and Tax Statement.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <p>Sign Here</p>
    <p>Signature</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <p>Purpose of form. Form 4852 serves as a substitute for Forms W-2, W-2c, and 1099-R and is completed by <span data-field="filer_name">{{ filer_name }}</span>. If you received an incorrect Form W-2 or Form 1099-R, you should always attempt to have your employer or payer correct the form before filing Form 4852.</p>
    <p>You should always attempt to get Form W-2 or Form 1099-R from your employer or payer before mailing this form. If you are unable to obtain the form, you may still use this form to report the information you have. If you are unable to obtain the form, you may still use this form to report the information you have.</p>
    <p>For Privacy Act and Paperwork Reduction Act Notice, see page 2.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p>Form 4852 (Rev. 12-2005)</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>Instructions</p>
    <p>Lines 1-3. Enter your name, social security number (SSN) and current address including street, city, state, and ZIP code.</p>
    <p>Line 4. Enter the year you received taxable income from Form W-2 or Form 1099-R. If you received not was received.</p>
    <p>Line 5. Enter your employer's or payer's name, address, and ZIP code.</p>
    <p>Line 6. Enter your employer's or payer's identification number, if known.</p>
    <p>Line 7(A) Form W-2. Enter wages, tips, other compensation, and taxes withheld.</p>
    <p>Line 7(B) Form 1099-R. Enter distributions from pensions, annuities, retirement/profit-sharing plans, IRAs, insurance contracts, etc.</p>
    <p>Line 8. How did you determine the amounts in lines 7(A) and 7(B) above?</p>
    <p>Line 9. Explain your efforts to obtain Form W-2, Form 1099-R, or Form W-2C, Corrected Wage and Tax Statement.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <p>Taxable amount not determined. Mark an "X" in this box if you are unable to compute your taxable distribution. If you are unable to compute your taxable distribution, you must use the amount shown on line 1 as a total distribution.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>Total distribution. Mark an "X" in this box only if the payment shown on line 1 is a total distribution.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>Capital gain (included in 2a). Enter the capital gain on the distribution. You also include any amounts that are not included in the taxable amount. See the instructions for Form 4972. Taxable amount not determined. See the instructions for Form 4972.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>Federal income tax withheld. Enter the amount of federal income tax withheld.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>State income tax withheld. Enter the amount of state income tax withheld.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>Local income tax withheld. Enter the amount of local income tax withheld.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>Employee contributions. Enter your investment in the distribution, if any. If you received no employee contributions, enter 0.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>Distribution codes. Enter the distribution codes from Form 1099-R, if applicable. If you received no distribution codes, enter 0.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <p>Privacy Act and Paperwork Reduction Act Notice. We ask for the information on Form 4852 only to carry out the internal functions of the Internal Revenue Service. You are required to provide this information to the IRS to carry out its functions. You may request a copy of this form from the IRS. You may request a copy of this form from the IRS. You may request a copy of this form from the IRS.</p>
    <p>If you receive an incorrect Form W-2 or Form 1099-R, you should always attempt to have your employer or payer correct the form before filing Form 4852.</p>
    <p>We also disclose this information to other countries and foreign governments as required by law. We may also disclose this information to other countries and foreign governments as required by law.</p>
    <p>The average time and expenses required to complete and file Form 4852 is <span data-field="avg_time">{{ avg_time }}</span>. The average time and expenses required to complete and file Form 4852 is <span data-field="avg_expenses">{{ avg_expenses }}</span>.</p>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>